# show ip pim neighbor (Cisco IOS and IOS-XE)
#
# An example operator template for axlib parse: ntc-templates has none for
# this command.  The file name, <platform>_<command with _ for spaces>.textfsm,
# is all axlib needs to use it; no index file is required.
#
# Key marks the fields that identify a neighbor, so `axlib parse diff` can
# report "this neighbor's mode changed" instead of "one removed, one added".
# Uptime/Expires changes every time the command runs, so the rule matches it
# with \S+/\S+ but does not capture it: a value that is never recorded can
# never show up as a difference.
Value Key NEIGHBOR (\d+\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+)
Value Key INTERFACE (\S+)
Value VERSION (v\d)
Value DR_PRIORITY (\d+)
Value MODE (\S.*?)

Start
  ^PIM\s+Neighbor\s+Table
  ^Mode:
  ^\s+[A-Z]+\s+-\s+
  ^Neighbor\s+Interface
  ^Address\s+Prio/Mode
  ^${NEIGHBOR}\s+${INTERFACE}\s+\S+/\S+\s+${VERSION}\s+${DR_PRIORITY}\s*/\s*${MODE}\s*$$ -> Record
  ^${NEIGHBOR}\s+${INTERFACE}\s+\S+/\S+\s+${VERSION}\s+${DR_PRIORITY}\s*/?\s*$$ -> Record
  ^\s*$$
  ^. -> Error
